Sat Oct 24 04:46:20 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.10.2:
  * CVE-2026-8712: SSRF via malicious uri query parameter in the
    HTTP API let unauthenticated attackers force outbound
    connections to arbitrary targets (boo#1278078)
  * HTTP servers now require --uri or --allow-uri-override, restrict
    request URIs to tcp:// and unix://, and no longer return
    exception details to clients
  * Upstream project moved from rhasspy to the OHF-Voice
    organization; update URL and source accordingly
  * Add VAD and audio preferences to ASR, select-program support,
    transcript names/terms, and text_format for synthesize
  * Add intents-start/end events, user events, wake_words query
    parameter, and home control flag for handle
  * Streaming support for tts, handle and asr; bi-directional
    run-pipeline with wake word names and announce text
  * Fix ZeroConf discovery, 8-bit audio conversion, and stop
    servers gracefully on SIGTERM
  * Migrate to pyproject.toml and support Python 3.13
- Spec cleanup: drop obsolete Group tag and tighten the file list

